#: src/languages/markdown.md:3
msgid "Markdown"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:5
msgid "Markdown support is available natively in Zed."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:7
msgid ""
"Tree-sitter: [tree-sitter-markdown](https://github.com/tree-sitter-grammars/"
"tree-sitter-markdown)"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:8
msgid "Language Server: N/A"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:10
msgid "Syntax Highlighting Code Blocks"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:12
msgid ""
"Zed supports language-specific syntax highlighting of markdown code blocks "
"by leveraging [tree-sitter language grammars](../extensions/languages."
"md#grammar). All [Zed supported languages](../languages.md), including those "
"provided by official or community extensions, are available for use in "
"markdown code blocks. All you need to do is provide a language name after "
"the opening <kbd>\\```</kbd> code fence like so:"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:24
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:26
msgid "Format"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:28
msgid ""
"Zed supports using Prettier to automatically re-format Markdown documents. "
"You can trigger this manually via the <code class=\"hljs\">editor: format</"
"code> action or via the <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-shift-i|ctrl-shift-i</"
"kbd> keyboard shortcut. Alternately, you can enable format on save."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:30
msgid ""
"Configure formatting in Settings (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-,|ctrl-,</"
"kbd>) under Languages > Markdown, or add to your settings file:"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:33 src/languages/markdown.md:53
#: src/languages/markdown.md:67 src/languages/markdown.md:81
msgid "\"languages\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:34 src/languages/markdown.md:54
#: src/languages/markdown.md:68 src/languages/markdown.md:82
msgid "\"Markdown\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:35
msgid "\"format_on_save\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:35
msgid "\"on\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:40
msgid "List Continuation"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:42
msgid ""
"Zed automatically continues lists when you press Enter at the end of a list "
"item. Supported list types:"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:44
msgid "Unordered lists (`-`, `*`, or `+` markers)"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:45
msgid "Ordered lists (numbers are auto-incremented)"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:46
msgid "Task lists (`- [ ]` and `- [x]`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:48
msgid ""
"Pressing Enter on an empty list item removes the marker and exits the list."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:50 src/languages/markdown.md:64
msgid ""
"To disable this behavior, configure in Settings (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-,|ctrl-,</kbd>) under Languages > Markdown, or add "
"to your settings file:"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:55
msgid "\"extend_list_on_newline\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:60
msgid "List Indentation"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:62
msgid ""
"Zed indents list items when you press Tab while the cursor is on a line "
"containing only a list marker. This allows you to quickly create nested "
"lists."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:69
msgid "\"indent_list_on_tab\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:74
msgid "Trailing Whitespace"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:76
msgid ""
"By default Zed will remove trailing whitespace on save. If you rely on "
"invisible trailing whitespace being converted to `<br />` in Markdown files "
"you can disable this behavior."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:78
msgid ""
"Configure in Settings (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-,|ctrl-,</kbd>) under "
"Languages > Markdown, or add to your settings file:"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/markdown.md:83
msgid "\"remove_trailing_whitespace_on_save\""
msgstr ""
